---
title: Creamy white chicken chili
servings: 7
tags: [american, chicken, weeknight, quick]
cuisine: american
time: 50 minutes
source: Creamy White Chili by Taste of Home, https://www.tasteofhome.com/recipes/creamy-white-chili
nutrition:
  calories: 334 kcal
  fat: 16 g
  saturated fat: 8 g
  carbohydrates: 24 g
  sugar: 3 g
  protein: 22 g
  fiber: 7 g
  sodium: 1045 mg
---

Heat the @canola oil{1%tbsp} in a #saucepan{}. Cook the
@chicken breasts{1%lb}(in 1/2 inch cubes), @onion{1}(chopped) and
@garlic powder{1%tsp} until the chicken is no longer pink.

Add the @canned white beans{31%oz}(great northern, two 15 1/2 oz cans, rinsed and drained),
@chicken broth{14.5%oz}(one can), @canned green chiles{8%oz}(two 4 oz cans, chopped),
@salt{1%tsp}, @ground cumin{1%tsp}, @dried oregano{1%tsp},
@black pepper{1%tsp} and @cayenne pepper{1/4%tsp}.

Bring to a boil, then simmer uncovered ~{30%minutes}.

Take off the heat and stir in the @sour cream{1%cup} and
@heavy whipping cream{1/2%cup}.

Serve topped with @?tortilla chips{}, @?cheddar cheese{}(shredded) and
@?jalapeno{}(seeded, sliced).
